{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>For what does the wise man have more.</b> If the wise man seeks money without end, and his soul is not satisfied — like the soul of the fool — what advantage does he have?" "<b>And the meaning of \"what does the poor man know.\"</b> The poor man who knows and understands — what does he have to walk in the way of fools?" "<b>Before the living.</b> \"Living\" in this place is an adjective, like \"all of you are living.\""], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:56.990421938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}